<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><subtitle type="html">FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:55:12Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Middle East live: US destroys five Iranian oil tankers as Iran threatens Kuwait and Bahrain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:99b23bec5d4d1c1fde7c96c4fe627b0d18a9b7359d3c1eae5276be4e280d2899</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:55:03Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T23:07:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260908-middle-east-live-us-destroys-five-iranian-oil-tankers-as-iran-threatens-kuwait-and-bahrain--06fb925ebc76.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260908-middle-east-live-us-destroys-five-iranian-oil-tankers-as-iran-threatens-kuwait-and-bahrain" /><summary type="html">US forces destroyed five Iranian oil carriers on Tuesday after Tehran launched ballistic missiles at an American warship twice in recent days. Iran also launched strikes on US targets in Jordan, and threatened attacks on oil tankers off Kuwait and Bahrain. Follow our liveblog for the latest updates.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>UK, France, ⁠Canada sanction Israeli West Bank goods</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:19a33fcfaafa04d61b338f54f487ae05d95c8477dade50410d407392169e6208</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:55:12Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T21:02:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260908-uk-france-canada-sanction-israeli-west-bank-goods--fdacae129b44.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260908-uk-france-canada-sanction-israeli-west-bank-goods" /><summary type="html">Israel said on Tuesday it was closing Britain's consulate in East Jerusalem in response to plans by the UK, France and Canada to block imports from Israeli settlements in the West Bank. FRANCE 24's Sharon Gaffney speaks with Julie Norman, Associate Fellow with the Middle East and North Africa Programme at Chatham House and Director of UCL’s Israel-Palestine Initiative.</summary><category term="A propos" /></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu under fire over report UAE warned of October 7 attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a6d992914c019533b2ce76a2eb7d02759b92f5497d689a9bf6ba0058c9f44db6</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T18:31:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/netanyahu-under-fire-over-report-uae-warned-of-october-7-attack--7fd6213c811c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/netanyahu-under-fire-over-report-uae-warned-of-october-7-attack" /><summary type="html">Israeli opposition leaders on Tuesday called Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu unfit to serve after a report that the United Arab Emirates had warned him before the October 7, 2023 Hamas attack. Haaretz newspaper, in a report excerpted from a forthcoming book by its reporters, said UAE President Mohamed bin Zayed Al Nahyan spoke to Netanyahu a week and a half before the attack and told him that Hamas was planning a major operation. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>UK, France, Canada to ban imports from Israeli settlements</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:15e56af5c4be8ee5fe8eedff06b2a7e763dbd20a870caf7b3b57f8832ba74d82</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T18:24:32Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/uk-france-canada-to-ban-imports-from-israeli-settlements--5103789d99a3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/uk-france-canada-to-ban-imports-from-israeli-settlements" /><summary type="html">Britain, France and Canada said Tuesday they will ban imports from Israeli settlements in the occupied West Bank, with a UK minister accusing Israel of turning a blind eye to the "ethnic cleansing" of Palestinians there. FRANCE 24's Emerald Maxwell reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>US war on Iran: 'Incompetent administration when it comes to negotiations and prosecuting war'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5fc69536b64c4f6308b73d0c7024605eb1d31a410117fcf384d3ec0e56bb5b45</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T16:16:16Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-war-on-iran-incompetent-administration-when-it-comes-to-negotiations-and-prosecuting-war--1e3a59faed45.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-war-on-iran-incompetent-administration-when-it-comes-to-negotiations-and-prosecuting-war" /><summary type="html">Mark Owen is pleased to welcome Barbara Slavin, Distinguished Fellow at the Simpson Center. She frames the war in the Persian Gulf as a mutually damaging stalemate in which neither Washington nor Tehran has found a politically sustainable exit: "There are no winners in this war". Her central argument is that the conflict has created a problem of face-saving as much as military strategy. The US faces rising economic and electoral costs, while Iran confronts shortages, inflation, domestic dissent and intensified repression. Neither side, in her assessment, can plausibly claim success.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel to close British consulate in Jerusalem after sanctions on settlements</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:66595961144ff6edc6781caef957b3446c943914b94fa62931e87bf0d08c7b67</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T15:10:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260908-middle-east-live-israel-to-close-british-consulate-in-jerusalem-after-sanctions-on-settleme--6854a83facb6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260908-middle-east-live-israel-to-close-british-consulate-in-jerusalem-after-sanctions-on-settlements" /><summary type="html">British Foreign Secretary Ed Miliband accused the Israeli government on Tuesday of turning a "blind eye" to what he called "ethnic cleansing" by settlers in the West Bank as the UK joined France and ten other countries in banning imports from Israeli settlements in the occupied territory. The decision comes amid rising violence over settlement expansion. Follow our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>France, UK to join 10 other countries in banning goods from Israeli West Bank settlements</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3ed43722e85a2bb33373b7d8d47f72513a4f8e8c35195c696b849286cb2a2e34</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T12:54:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260908-france-and-canada-to-join-uk-in-banning-goods-from-israeli-west-bank-settlements--b760488b9f5e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260908-france-and-canada-to-join-uk-in-banning-goods-from-israeli-west-bank-settlements" /><summary type="html">France is preparing to introduce a ban on products from Israeli settlements in the occupied West Bank, Foreign Minister Jean-Noël ​Barrot said on Tuesday, following a wave of settler violence in recent days that has further undermined prospects for a two-state solution with the Palestinians. France has joined the UK and ten other countries in announcing the trade ban on goods, and some services, from Israeli settlements.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>UAE leader warned Netanyahu of Hamas attack days before October 7, says report</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f9b85326f31be17dc09fb67ff9f022263c31dc01efcb69dd0570082abe38cf14</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T09:40:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260908-uae-leader-warned-netanyahu-of-hamas-attack-days-before-october-7-says-report--a3829f73dcb9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260908-uae-leader-warned-netanyahu-of-hamas-attack-days-before-october-7-says-report" /><summary type="html">Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu faced strong backlash from opposition leaders on Tuesday after a report published by Haaretz newspaper said UAE President Mohamed bin Zayed Al Nahyan warned Netanyahu that Hamas was planning a major operation days before the attacks on October 7. The report alleges that Netanyahu failed to inform security chiefs.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Houthi attacks disrupt Saudi oil facilities and wound more than 70</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8e67904e3ebc65dc137dc74a649a152124918e0740246ea4454b831ef2bfe7c7</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T09:14:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260908-houthi-attacks-disrupt-saudi-oil-facilities-and-wound-more-than-70--ed16b49517da.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260908-houthi-attacks-disrupt-saudi-oil-facilities-and-wound-more-than-70" /><summary type="html">Houthi forces attacked four cities in southern Saudi Arabia on Tuesday, wounding at least 73 people and setting oil facilities ablaze in one of the largest assaults on the US ally since the wider Gulf war began. The strikes came as explosions were reported at Iran’s Kharg Island and the Gulf of Oman port of ​Jask, raising fears of renewed US attacks and further escalation.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel intensifies south Lebanon strikes, killing 13 after weeks-long lull</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:653a3d98049f5867b3dc7f22d5a8a7110ac64eef5416f4ac6cd909feb9ead238</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T21:32:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260907-israeli-strikes-south-lebanon-violence--1ad7641e3826.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260907-israeli-strikes-south-lebanon-violence" /><summary type="html">Israel launched a wave of air strikes across southern Lebanon, killing 13 people, including women and children, Lebanon’s health ministry said on Monday, marking an escalation after weeks of relative calm. Israel said it would continue targeting Iran-backed Hezbollah over alleged ceasefire violations. Hezbollah has not commented on the strikes.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel warns of 'full-scale war' if Palestinian Authority launches Oct. 7-style attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3880871c6129618d158bd3cfd9131041c07b5c1decf2d2deef04db57a5f9f979</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T18:08:40Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260907-israel-warns-of-full-scale-war-if-palestinian-authority-launches-oct-7-style-attack--e5884b7104de.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260907-israel-warns-of-full-scale-war-if-palestinian-authority-launches-oct-7-style-attack" /><summary type="html">Israel on Monday threatened a “full-scale war” against the Palestinian Authority if it believed the West Bank-based body was preparing an attack on Israeli forces or settlements resembling Hamas’s October 7, 2023 assault. The warning was denounced by Palestinian authorities as an attempt to fuel the conflict during the Israeli election season.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli strikes on southern Lebanon kill 11</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f587cbef30a999f318245b1359326c960432d81cce0d8db561dc771f85761d0e</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T14:10:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-israeli-strikes-on-southern-lebanon-kill-11--4d2222e87b6b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260907-israeli-strikes-on-southern-lebanon-kill-11" /><summary type="html">Israeli strikes ⁠on a ​southern Lebanese town early on Monday killed at least 11 people including two children ​and two medics, Lebanon's state news agency said. Israel has intensified its bombardment of south Lebanon in recent days despite a June ceasefire that was meant ​to halt fighting ‌between the Israeli military and Lebanese armed ⁠group Hezbollah.</summary></entry><entry><title>UN rapporteur says Israeli rubble-clearing in Gaza could erase 'atrocity crimes' evidence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:003f17360050be467662f683ffe732c760edeca598abcbeb0d9083a74a049f46</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T12:51:23Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260907-un-rapporteur-says-israeli-rubble-clearing-in-gaza-could-erase-atrocity-crimes-evidence--bf0ebb6f2138.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260907-un-rapporteur-says-israeli-rubble-clearing-in-gaza-could-erase-atrocity-crimes-evidence" /><summary type="html">The United Nations Special Rapporteur Francesca Albanese warned on Monday that the large-scale rubble removal in parts of Gaza under Israeli control could risk erasing "evidence relevant to the investigation of alleged international crimes".</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Several killed in Israeli strikes in southern Lebanon</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2fb1665abbad1677011420da3fdce9cdd5898248083373a6a33eae616d302945</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-07T01:13:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260907-middle-east-live-israel-army-orders-evacuation-of-zone-in-south-lebanon-ahead-of-strikes--2806097dc20d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260907-middle-east-live-israel-army-orders-evacuation-of-zone-in-south-lebanon-ahead-of-strikes" /><summary type="html">At ⁠least ​11 ​people were killed, including two infants, were injured ⁠in Israeli strikes on ​a ‌residential building in ‌a town ​in southern Lebanon early on Monday, ​Lebanon's ​state ​news agency ​reported. The Israeli army had demanded early Monday that residents of Deir Zahrani in southern Lebanon leave a specific zone ahead of strikes against Iran-backed Hezbollah. Follow our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli strikes kill four in Lebanon after alleged Hezbollah drone launch</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3f092c7b5f51c788e024a04ac5e9f543b4ebc14bf865310817e33798dddffbcb</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-06T08:49:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260906-israeli-strikes-kill-four-in-lebanon-after-alleged-hezbollah-drone-launch--d3c0c1b9e0a9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260906-israeli-strikes-kill-four-in-lebanon-after-alleged-hezbollah-drone-launch" /><summary type="html">Israeli air strikes on southern Lebanon Sunday killed four people, two of them women, the country's health ministry said. Israel's military said that the strikes were a response to an alleged Hezbollah drone launch targeting troops in the Israeli-occupied "security zone" in the country's south.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>US ambassador to Israel visits Palestinian town hit by West Bank settler violence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d5c49175aa5071655f44f35a9570da6eaf91ed018f47e840ae8996f0f0e291ea</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T12:19:19Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260905-us-ambassador-to-israel-visits-palestinian-town-hit-by-west-bank-settler-violence--9088e5f15b75.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260905-us-ambassador-to-israel-visits-palestinian-town-hit-by-west-bank-settler-violence" /><summary type="html">US ambassador to Israel Mike Huckabee on Saturday visited Turmus Ayya, a Palestinian town in the Israeli-occupied West Bank that has been repeatedly targeted by Israeli settler violence. Huckabee, a staunch supporter of Israel and its illegal settlements in the Palestinian territory, said that it was in the Israeli government's interests to take action against violent settlers.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>US military says it struck 3 Iranian oil tankers after missile attacks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:48f2917a08742188ae3d92b72e69e185e9b0ee5f985af866567327f94bac30e9</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-05T05:01:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260905-middle-east-live-israeli-strikes-on-south-and-east-lebanon-kill-three-people--9a0ff2430b05.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260905-middle-east-live-israeli-strikes-on-south-and-east-lebanon-kill-three-people" /><summary type="html">The US military said on Saturday it had struck and destroyed three Iranian oil tankers after Navy warships were targeted with missiles, adding that no American personnel ​were ​harmed. Earlier, Tehran accused the US of attacking an Iranian tanker near Kharg Island in the Persian Gulf, a key oil terminal. Follow our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israel's West Bank camp displacements could be crime against humanity, UN says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b49685cee338bfd79bc0815fc780737992b945217e11732764fe8fe046fc1609</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T16:26:55Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260904-israel-s-west-bank-camp-displacements-could-be-crime-against-humanity-un-says--03f625c09b2d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260904-israel-s-west-bank-camp-displacements-could-be-crime-against-humanity-un-says" /><summary type="html">The Israeli government's forced displacement of the entire populations of three West Bank refugee camps in January 2025 could amount to crimes against humanity, a UN report warned Friday. More than 33,000 Palestinians forced out of the Jenin, Nur Shams and Tulkarm camps have not been permitted to return home. Israel slammed the report for "spreading misinformation".</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli army has seized Lebanon's key Ali al-Taher ridge from Hezbollah</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:abd24f61d62b0eeabfe88f6cd509c5f5685e8b88e43b3f6fa49a8f1ec4174be4</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T13:27:50Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260904-israel-says-it-has-seized-lebanon-key-ali-al-taher-ridge-from-hezbollah--71676c0b7359.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260904-israel-says-it-has-seized-lebanon-key-ali-al-taher-ridge-from-hezbollah" /><summary type="html">Israel has seized the strategically placed Ali al-Taher ridge in southern Lebanon from Hezbollah fighters, Defence Minister Israel Katz said Friday. The Iran-aligned Shiite group did not confirm losing the highland, which sits around 10 kilometres from the border with Israel and was pummelled by Israeli strikes in recent weeks despite a ceasefire.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>New fears of oil supply disruption as US-Iran hostilities resume</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:348948373838ff8703b95d7ab9950fcc706a5edc50c190abcecf33c09689df7d</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T09:56:46Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-new-fears-of-oil-supply-disruption-as-us-iran-hostilities-resume--0869871bdd37.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260904-new-fears-of-oil-supply-disruption-as-us-iran-hostilities-resume" /><summary type="html">Renewed hostilities between the United States and Iran have brought back fears of oil supply disruption. Prices are on track for their steepest weekly gain since mid-July, up 7.6%, as the US-Iran war enters its seventh month. Twenty-five percent of the world's oil supply comes through the Strait of Hormuz, which has been blocked since the beginning of the war. FRANCE 24's international affairs editor Philip Turle gives more details.</summary></entry><entry><title>Trump says Iran war is 'small potatoes', Israel strikes southern Lebanon</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fea1d30d28c3180949028e458bd50bd8fc34d9b882738a2a92ac9a2014d40e5e</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-04T02:56:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260904-middle-east-live-south-korea-prepares-for-military-deployment-in-strait-of-hormuz--7d0e3110ee0d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260904-middle-east-live-south-korea-prepares-for-military-deployment-in-strait-of-hormuz" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump on Friday said the Iran war was "small potatoes" for the US, a day after Vice President JD Vance said he wouldn't describe the conflict as a war. In Lebanon, an Israeli strike killed two people in the south, state media reported. Read about the day’s events as they unfolded on our liveblog.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>No, UN chief Guterres did not call Francesca Albanese 'out of control'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ba208e548acbc36096c2a64f5bdcfc7ee404b278e39738329feec5800eca50db</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T19:34:29Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20260903-no-un-chief-guterres-did-not-call-francesca-albanese-out-of-control--dd310962b9f5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/truth-or-fake/20260903-no-un-chief-guterres-did-not-call-francesca-albanese-out-of-control" /><summary type="html">Pro-Israel lobby group UN Watch has alleged that UN Secretary-General Antonio Guterres referred to Francesca Albanese, the UN's Special Rapporteur on Palestine, as "out of control", saying he'd previously called her a "horrible woman". But Guterres named no one in his remarks. He said "many" independent rapporteurs were "totally out of control", without singling out any individual. The UN has since said that linking the comment specifically to Albanese is a "misreading" of his remarks. Vedika Bahl fact-checks.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>Anti-Christian murder in Syria? No indication he was killed because of his faith</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f195089018ece131a59eb56b02e52fb4fd501e5aa82671126e5f1a17f690912a</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T17:00:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-anti-christian-murder-syria-no-indication-killed-faith--cf972620ce2d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-anti-christian-murder-syria-no-indication-killed-faith" /><summary type="html">A Christian man by the name of Nader Boulos Tannous was murdered in Homs, Syria on August 15, 2026. After his death, Israel, Greece and Cyprus were quick to denounce what they called an anti-Christian act. Several days later however, authorities in Homs said the suspect had admitted killing Tannous as part of a personal dispute going back to 2012.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli attacks in West Bank at 'unprecedented' level, PNI leader Barghouti says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ef5e9bf515686c4dcdc9d29a9c82f3586fcf1997e22b75320f98b8a5f317a524</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T13:26:12Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t_te-_-t_te/20260903-israeli-attacks-in-west-bank-at-unprecedented-level-pni-leader-barghouti-says--38c73f0a94fa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20260903-israeli-attacks-in-west-bank-at-unprecedented-level-pni-leader-barghouti-says" /><summary type="html">In an interview with FRANCE 24, the secretary general of the Palestinian National Initiative (PNI) party Mustafa Barghouti said the level of Israeli attacks on Palestinians in the West Bank had become "totally unprecedented". With tensions escalating, activists accuse settlers of operating with total impunity. "Their goal is clear: it is ethnic cleansing," Barghouti stated, calling Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu's reaction to the attacks hypocritical.</summary><category term="Tête à tête" /></entry><entry><title>Has Iran modified its rocket systems to fire mines into the Strait of Hormuz?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b23621f2d5913b0660606db4734a5c13fd0fced23bb2f076ba914b0bfb57d7b5</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T05:57:20Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-has-iran-modified-its-rocket-systems-to-fire-mines-into-the-strait-of-hormuz--d9050c0ecfa3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-has-iran-modified-its-rocket-systems-to-fire-mines-into-the-strait-of-hormuz" /><summary type="html">Fighting escalated in the Middle East over the weekend after US airstrikes on Sunday targeted Iranian rocket launchers on the island of Larak. The exchange of fire was instigated by the US in retaliation against Iran’s new capabilities for firing mines from rockets into the Strait of Hormuz. Iran’s use of rocket launchers to deploy sea mines into the strategic waterway would be unprecedented, but not implausible. Even so, some analysts remain sceptical.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iran hits US targets in Mideast, wedding strikes being probed, Vance says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7ab34fec54fc1b4b9552cc89253eb379757c8d627d5ea0189757cf2e473fee43</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T05:19:13Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-iran-hits-us-targets-as-washington-says-probing-wedding-strike--e1bf83f56bbc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-iran-hits-us-targets-as-washington-says-probing-wedding-strike" /><summary type="html">Iran said on Thursday it hit US military bases in Kuwait and the UAE in retaliation for a US strike on a wedding party that killed four people and injured nearly 70. While the US military has reiterated that it never targets civilians, Vice President JD Vance said the strike was being investigated.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Toppling Iran’s Islamic regime ‘within reach’, Netanyahu says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:976ecaf97c152021ee720b547a65d83e8f10bebd8e56ed0b83655ace1b49f2bc</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T03:08:01Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-mideast-live-kuwait-army-says-intercepting-missile-drone-attack-from-iran--67d09afbe2b3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-mideast-live-kuwait-army-says-intercepting-missile-drone-attack-from-iran" /><summary type="html">Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu on Thursday voiced confidence that Iran's Islamic republic could soon fall, saying it was weaker than ever. Earlier, Iran's army said it targeted US bases in the UAE and Kuwait. Follow our liveblog to see how the day's events unfolded.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Iran, US trade threats as Tehran blames Washington for wedding strike</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4226e5cd12960ab095dc3a867ad4004e19abe8fb77de8a842ee50958a44cbc01</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-03T01:22:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-iran-us-trade-threats-wedding-strike--7495f90c90eb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20260903-iran-us-trade-threats-wedding-strike" /><summary type="html">Iran and the United States traded threats on Wednesday after their heaviest military exchanges in weeks. Tehran accused Washington of striking a wedding party and called the attack a war crime. President Donald Trump threatened further US strikes, while Iran’s security chief warned Washington would face a “new strategy.”</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>US-Iran war: Old videos falsely claim to show new attacks on American bases</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5374938687be7ba398cc18b272966da4d1b83fb0018243b31554f9ee0aed8e23</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:02Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T20:57:27Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/us-iran-war-old-videos-falsely-claim-to-show-new-attacks-on-american-bases-1--e29deba63932.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/us-iran-war-old-videos-falsely-claim-to-show-new-attacks-on-american-bases-1" /><summary type="html">As US-Iran hostilities flare up and strikes resume, so has a wave of misinformation online. Old and unrelated videos are flooding social media, falsely presented as footage of new attacks. As tensions escalate, clips filmed in Dubai, Russia and the US have been misrepresented as Iranian strikes on US bases in the Gulf. Elsewhere, a 68-year-old video of a US nuclear test has been falsely claimed to show Iran detonating mines in the Strait of Hormuz. Vedika Bahl fact-checks in Truth or Fake.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry></feed>
